    correct: 'C',
    explanation: "Modern demographic historians estimate that between 30–50% of Europe's population died during the initial outbreak of the Black Death between 1347 and 1353 — one of the deadliest demographic catastrophes in human history. Some regions lost more than half their population; others less.",
